Junwen Zhou  is an assistant professor at Beijing Institute of Technology. He received his BS in materials chemistry in 2010 and PhD in inorganic chemistry in 2015 from Peking University. His current research interests focus on functional porous materials, composites and membranes/films for emerging electrochemical energy storage technologies, such as lithium– sulfur batteries and lithium–air batteries.
Yu Dong  obtained her bachelor degree from Minzu University of China in 2016. Currently, she is a third-year Master student in the group of Prof. Bo Wang at Beijing Institute of Technology. Her research interests focus on lithium–air batteries.
